From: Moto E32 kernel analysis
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: lld: place Clang CFI jump tables in core text

With CONFIG_LTO_CLANG, Clang 11 emits CFI jump tables in input sections named
.text..L.cfi.jumptable and .text..L.cfi.jumptable.*.  The existing TEXT_MAIN
and TEXT_CFI_MAIN patterns do not match the double-dot suffix, so LLD places
these executable orphan sections before the output .text section and before
_stext.  CONFIG_DEBUG_NOTIFIERS then rejects notifier callback pointers to
those tables because func_ptr_is_kernel_text() only accepts _stext.._etext.

Collect the jump-table sections explicitly into .text.  This keeps the table
entries inside core_kernel_text()'s accepted range without disabling CFI.

---
 include/asm-generic/vmlinux.lds.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/include/asm-generic/vmlinux.lds.h b/include/asm-generic/vmlinux.lds.h
--- a/include/asm-generic/vmlinux.lds.h
+++ b/include/asm-generic/vmlinux.lds.h
@@ -465,5 +465,6 @@
 		*(.text..refcount)					\
 		*(.text..ftrace)					\
 		*(TEXT_CFI_MAIN) 					\
+		*(.text..L.cfi.jumptable .text..L.cfi.jumptable.*) \
 		*(.ref.text)						\
 	MEM_KEEP(init.text)						\
